/-!
# Conjugate non-normalization: source reductions and normalized planes

The original quotient, relative-component normality, Sylow point orbit,
commuting-conjugate radical containment, and numerical deductions are checked.
Reciprocal small-action recognition is proved in both the SL3 and Sp4 rows,
including the entire original nonsplit cover. The actual normalized-pair actor
also supplies plane alignment. These results exclude all small symmetric actions
under the original abelian-span and numerical hypotheses.

The proper-displacement, exact fixed-plane, centralizer-generation and
outside-radical calculations are proved. `conclusions_of_earlier_source`
assembles all three 11.2.4 conclusions, and `obstruction_of_earlier_source`
applies non-normalization to the actual critical pair for 11.2.5.
The original SL3 condition and authorized earlier numerical, first-line,
component and flag premises remain explicit for the final source owner.
No local geometric callback remains in these two exports.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, 11.2.4--5, printed pp.769--770.
-/
